comments.content:
ADDITIONAL SHAPE/FIXTURE FAN-OUT (same blocker; measured before any edit).

Correcting the live source reader creates an unavoidable test-fixture consequence also missing from every affectedFiles roster. release-handoff-test-harness.ts:443-456 defines seedArtifactManifest and passes identity.attemptAggregateId directly to the low-level sealer; seedReleaseHandoffSources calls it at :470. Every HandoffSeedIdentity currently carries the activation aggregate. That fixed-point fixture is consumed at:
- release-handoff-builder.test.ts:337,393,405,445,524;
- attempt-release-disposition.test.ts:343,1426;
- attempt-finalization-test-harness.ts:276;
and seedArtifactManifest directly at release-handoff-sources.test.ts:185 and foundation-attempt-service.test.ts:1030.

If production sources.ts is corrected to query the dispatch-keyed writer row while this harness keeps seeding only the activation-keyed row, the builder/source/finalization/release suites refuse ABSENT. Seeding BOTH would preserve the old tautology and make a reader-regression mutant green. The shared fixture must instead seed exactly deriveDispatchAggregateId(identity.attemptAggregateId), matching foundation-attempt-store's real writer. Owning only builder.test.ts cannot honestly repair the whole consumer fan-out.

Amendment therefore also needs apps/daemon/src/work/release-handoff-test-harness.ts as an owned path (and the focused gate should cover release-handoff-sources.test.ts or explicitly include the full daemon leg). This remains under the task's file-count cap. No other active task names either required path.
